# Azog, Moria's Ruin: "destroy up to one other target creature". Azog itself is not a legal target (the refusal), though Bot2's Llanowar
# Elves is (the positive control: it is among the choices of the very same question); and "up to one" lets Bot1 choose nothing, in which
# case the Elves lives and no one amasses or draws.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Azog, Moria's Ruin
Plains x3
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Azog, Moria's Ruin.Cast
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Azog, Moria's Ruin)
Bot1.Target()
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Azog, Moria's Ruin
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
